	(text "SeedJoy Test Board rev A - Seeed XIAO nRF52840 (non-Sense), all 3.3 V\nJ1 = XIAO left header (D0/A0 ... D6), J2 = XIAO right header (5V, GND, 3V3, D10, D9, D8, D7), USB-C at pin 1 end\n74HC165: SER tied to 3V3; pull-ups 10k to 3V3; buttons active-LOW (firmware Invert Logic ON). BTN1 = SR_IN0 = HID button 1\nSW9: 1=D4, 2=D5, 3=D10 (GPIO buttons; enabling any shifts SR buttons to 17+), 4=D9 MODE (ON at reset = BLE)\nX_SEL / Y_SEL: jumper row n routes stick axis to An (A0..A3). Never jumper X and Y to the same An.\nSTICK_BTN_EN: jumper puts the thumbstick push-button in parallel with BTN8"
		(at 38.1 231.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "bb996889-02fc-440a-830f-d0c9558df24a")
	)
	(text "J7 SR_CHAIN_IN: chain your own 74HC165 board here (3V3, GND, CLK, LOAD, SER-in).\nYour chain's last QH -> J7-5. Your chips become buttons 1..8N; this board's 8 buttons follow.\nSet \"Number of chips\" = N + 1. R1 pulls CHAIN_IN high when nothing is connected."
		(at 38.1 264.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "627dfd8d-96d1-4d6e-8007-d57d143cf244")
	)
